# SRG-APP-000029-AU-000610  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must automatically audit account removal actions.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000029-AU-000610
group:           V-221903
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-001405
control_rev5:    AC-2

contribution:    Splunk writes an audit event when a user object is removed, generation of
                 which is not configurable; the application's configurable share is that
                 those audit events are queued to an index, and that the edit_user
                 capability, which the specification states "lets a user create, edit, or
                 remove other users", is confined to the intended roles so each removal is
                 attributable.

governs:         audit.conf - The audit trail Splunk keeps of its own activity, and how those records
                 are signed.

check:           audit.conf [auditTrail] queueing not_equals false

external:        Removal of an identity from an external LDAP directory or SAML identity
                 provider is audited by that component; Splunk records only removals of
                 objects it holds.
external:        The role assignment of the edit_user capability in authorize.conf
                 [capability::edit_user] reflects an organizational access control
                 decision, and the product ships the capability with default role
                 assignments, so its absence from a local configuration file is not a
                 defect.
external:        Where audit queueing is false by design, an inputs.conf monitor stanza
                 tailing the audit log carries retention.

citation:        splunk-spec-files/audit.conf.spec:23-29 ([auditTrail] queueing =
                 <boolean>, default true); splunk-spec-files/authorize.conf.spec:719-721
                 ([capability::edit_user]); SRG-APP-000029-AU-000610 check and fix text.
finding:         Audit records for account removal are generated by Splunk but not retained
                 in an index, because audit.conf [auditTrail] queueing is set to false and
                 no compensating monitor input is configured; this is assessed at the
                 application layer alone, and removals performed in an external directory
                 service or identity provider are audited by that component, which is
                 recorded as an external dependency.
